    "result_text": "The full suite is green (11 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe `Cp05Tests` acceptance test creates an owner and reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, asserting `$.displayName` equals `\"LastName, FirstName\"`. The `OwnerDto` returned by both create and read is generated from `openapi.yml` and populated via a MapStruct mapper, so the fix has two parts:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it's serialized in responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct expression mapping that computes `displayName` as `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` from the stored names.\n\nThis keeps the value derived from the persisted `firstName`/`lastName` (not the request body) and applies uniformly to every owner response, matching the exact `'LastName, FirstName'` format. Full test suite: **11 passed, 0 failures**.",
